         <p>Volume responds immediately and attenuates the physical master knob: 0 mutes, 127 keeps the physical knob’s level. Computer playback follows <strong>USB VOLUME</strong> instead. Turning MIDI KNOBS OFF restores the physical master level. MIDI volume resets to full on power-on.</p>
         <p>USB, TRS and Bluetooth work identically. A channel admitted by ROUT controls the selected panel track, even when that channel’s notes play another track. Mapped CCs are consumed by the panel; they do not also change a synth parameter or pass through a MIDI Track. Other CCs retain their normal behavior. Set MIDI KNOBS OFF to keep all conventional CC behavior, including CC74 brightness and CC71 resonance. The MiniLab assignments are documented in <a href="https://support.arturia.com/hc/en-us/articles/6189475866396-MiniLab-3-General-Questions">Arturia’s MIDI implementation chart</a>.</p>
 
